# .deps is an unpacked toolchain: linux-deps.sh installs Zig, Wasmtime and
# Swift under /opt inside the image, but a contributor who ran --install on
# the host first has the same trees in .deps, and they are gigabytes of a
# context nothing in either Dockerfile reads. The prune lines in Dockerfile
# and Dockerfile.arch cover the same ground inside the tree; this is what
# keeps the copy from ever carrying them.
.deps
